<title>USA: ECRI monthly U.S. inflation gauge 105.9 in Dec.</title>
<headline>ECRI monthly U.S. inflation gauge 105.9 in Dec.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economic Cycle Research Institute (ECRI) monthly future inflation gauge (FIG) fell to 105.9 in December from a revised 106.0 the previous month, ECRI said.</p>
<p>The index fell as the insured unemployment rate rose and the yield spread between 10-year and three-month Treasuries widened, ECRI said.</p>
<p>The FIG &quot;is not yet close to triggering a signal of an upcoming inflation cycle upturn,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660))</p>
